Package: faofishingreport
Type: Package
Title: Analyse and Report FAO Global Capture Production Statistics
Version: 0.6.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Hongyu", "Lin", email = "linbojun99@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Rainer", "Froese", role = c("ctb", "cph"), comment = "CMSY++ code, neural network and user guide in inst/cmsy (CC BY 4.0)"),
    person("Gianpaolo", "Coro", role = c("ctb", "cph"), comment = "CMSY++ code in inst/cmsy"),
    person("Henning", "Winker", role = c("ctb", "cph"), comment = "CMSY++ code in inst/cmsy"),
    person("Nazli", "Demirel", role = c("ctb", "cph"), comment = "CMSY++ user guide in inst/cmsy"))
Description: Analyses FAO Global Capture Production statistics by fishing area,
    country and species, and exports charts (PNG and editable PowerPoint) and
    tables for reports. Includes breakpoint analysis of catch time series,
    checks for and downloads the latest FAO data release, and draws charts in
    English, Chinese or both, using official FAO Chinese names and a Chinese
    font chosen for the operating system. Runs the catch-only stock assessment
    method CMSY++ (Froese et al. 2023 <doi:10.3897/aiep.53.105910>) on the catch
    series, with the bundled CMSY++ code, priors from FishBase and SeaLifeBase,
    and JAGS installed and the code adapted for the operating system.
